From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:49:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] coherent: a copy back leaves a held batch's record;
 held batches copy in later writes through other imports (path 4)

Two defects behind the path-4 lanes (ebc8cb30), both losing writes Metal keeps:

- A GPU copy back (shadow_lazy's flush, for a command buffer that meets the bytes through
  another import, met_by) covered every running record (before_flush's through = seq). A
  command buffer waiting for a shared event has a batch the scheduler has not planned, which the
  tracker cannot order the copy after: the copy ran before it, flushed() marked its record done,
  its completion armed nothing, and its writes never reached the pages (the guest read the older
  bytes). Base lanes: every failing variant made exactly one copy back, both passing none.
  Now the scheduler notes each command buffer from its commit to the plan of its last batch
  (shadow_lazy::planned, under the scheduler's lock, one short lock), and a copy back covers the
  records up to the first one still unplanned: that one and those after it land at their
  completion as ever. flushed() takes the copy's mark apart from what it covered.
  Counted: flushes_held_back.
- Path 4, left by 6e193b3b: a standing taken after a wait knew nothing of a write of the
  surface's bytes through another import (a buffer over the pages, another texture's copy back)
  encoded after it and ordered before the signal. Each such write of a trapping surface is now
  kept with its command buffer and rectangle (Lazy's Beside, from note_writes, by the byte range
  against the truth's), and the held batch's late copy in also takes the rectangles written after
  its standing's count by command buffers the scheduler planned all of: the copy's uses join the
  batch's summary, so the tracker orders it after those writes, as Metal orders them before the
  batch by the event. A write not planned yet is ordered after the batch and left (counted
  late_beside_unplanned). A record still open or running over the rectangle is counted busy,
  as in taking_late (the own variants count one: the command buffer's own earlier pass).
  Proof that path 4 is its own defect: with the second fix off (first alone), the three buffer
  variants lose the other import's write at (9,100).

Counters: per surface late_copies, late_busy, late_compares, late_compare_ns(_max), late_beside;
a process line first in shadow_coherent::report (so coherent.jsonl carries it), with
late_copies_in(_busy), the snapshot compares (count, ns, max), late_beside(_unplanned),
flushes_held_back and the other fallbacks. A surface's line stays last.

Lanes (ANV): the six path-4 lanes fail 4/6 at bc15b13e and pass here; unit tests
tests::coherent_late (area of a byte range, the plan set).

